        <p>VLECTION 0 F CONIMISSIONERS. SEPTEMBER Tra. 13. TO THE OWNERS AND RATEPAYRRS OF RUNCORN.</p>
        <p>Lawns AND GLNTLEMt Pf, Although natives a Runcorn, it is with some diffi- dence that we resp-cfhilly solicit your sur.•rages at the elec- tion now pending for five gelatlemen to serve you on you Board of Co msnissioners. In submitting our names jointly for your considerationove do so as independent candidates absolutely free from any Pledges to person, party, or clique, our only aim being for carrying out loyally the provisions of the Improvement A.et as far as lies in our power, and making the said act ot some- thing of a reality. Suggestions have often been made to us, and we place them before you to give judgment upon at the poll, that the Board as at present constituted consists of several members who, in watching personal ints rests, entirely neglect the sanitation of the town. We feel strongly that all parts of the town Should have an equal amount of inspection and supervision from the Board's officials and employts, andtt at the regula. tions affecting building and sanitary arrangements of pro- ' Perty should be applied to allowners alike. We purposely refrain tram adopting ass " election cry," ' bec,ause promises at elections are, tts a rule, Impracticable,but we assure you if. you do us the honour of returning us as your representatives on the Commission, that the same energy, watchfulness, and careful attention that have been needed to establish and build up our reapective businesses shalt he placed unreserysdly at your disposal. We are Ladies andGentlamen. Faithfully yours, THOMAS lONNS. ARTHUR 'MUGU.</p>
