        <p>THEFT or Toots.—Mary Brown was charged with stealing a bas containing two hani:ners and other brick- layer.' tools, a shirt, and a jacket, the property of Joseph Collins on the previous day.—The complainant and de- fendant bad come from Oldham together on the previous day to look for work, and took lodgings as man and wife at Ship Yard. The complainant went out soon after- wards, and defendant went out with the tools and jacket. When complainant came back and missed the articles, he at once informed the police, and Detective Monaghan who had ascertained that defendant had offered several of the tools for pledge, met her in Mersey- ' st., and arrested her, All the articles were found.— Prisoner was committed for 14 days. TREY DROPPED THEM AND RAN.—Three boys, John Ring (14). John Cook (18), James King (13), were each charged with stealing two barrels valued Bd. from the A lady writes from Stockport, 17th April, 1899 : market on the previous night.—Detective Monaghan " Hoinocea 'is not known as it ought to be for skin stated that he was crossing Town Hill on the previous night and saw the three prisoners with the two barrels. disorders. I myself, have suffered very severely for forty-four years from Scurvy or Eczema left by small- When they saw witness they dropped them and ran, but pox. Have always been able to have first medical ad- Cook was captured. • The barrels were identified by Mrs. vice, bnt doctors have not been able to do all these years Locker and Mrs. Massey as their property.—The pri- soners said that there was no bottom in the barrels and what Homocea . has done in three weeks. My doctor they thought they were of no use.—The three prisoners is surprised at the result. I earnestly desire to assist • others to the relief I myself have received:" were ordered to be kept in the bridewell until six o'clock. - I Lord Combermere, Lord Carrick, Bishop Taylor, and Hamm AND DISORDERLY.—Joseph Smith who was very many others also bear witness to the marvellous effects good humoured during his trial, his face being wreathed of" Homocea.,' with smiles, was dismissed with a caution on this 66 H charge. omocea " sold by mist Chemists at"ls. 14i., and 2s. 9d. per box, or sent post free on receipt3of stamps CO EIGHTEEN ARTIFICIAL TEETEI KNOCKED OCT.—William Leigh, 9 Rose Court, Liverpool-road, was charged with 21, HAMILTON SQ., BIRKENHEAD.</p>
