        <p>CM:1E1100C V. WIDNES (SECOND Euvraws).—Played at Clubmoor cm Saturday. Score :—Widnes, 56 ; Club- moor, 69.</p>
        <p>MOORES V. Sr. ELPHIN'S (Wenntrwrros).—Played at Moore. on Saturday, and resulted in an env win for the Moore team by 13 runs. Score :—Moore, 81 ;St. Elphin's 48.</p>
        <p>Wenranavow V. Pinerrox.—This return match was played at Warrington. on Saturday. The visitcrs won the toss, and a little before two o'clock Messrs Harper and nest faced the deliveries of Messrs. S. M. Croakld and Bell. From the onset runs were put on at a fair pace, Best scoring the more rapidly, the total score being 196. Against.this formidable score Warrington gave a poor display, and although the wicket helped the bowl- ers a little, there is no excuse for the paltry score. With only a run on G. Clarke was bowled, whilst Voisey was sent back at eleven. With Messrs. Crosfield and Smith rested the last hopes of Warrington saving the game, but when these were dismissed at 25 and 43 respectively the match was considered as .good as over, and such proved to be the case, for Holmes carried everything before him, and the innings closed for 62, Holmes' last four overs showing six wickets for four runs. Score avid bowling analysis :</p>
