        <p>TO THE PROPERTY OWNERS AND RATE- PAYERS OF RUNCORN. LADIES AND GENTLEMEN, I have duly considered and decided not to seek re-election on the Board of Commissioners this year. Allow meto thank you very much for your kindness during the twelve years I have had the privilege of representing you on that Board. Believe me. Yours very faithfully. WILLIAM FISHER. The Nooks, Higher Runcorn, August 31st, 1893.</p>
        <p>ELECTION OF COMMISSIONERS. Thursday, September 7th, 1893. TO THE RATEPAYERS OP RUNCORN. LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,— The term for which I was elected as one of your re- presentatives has expired, and I now respectfully offer my- self as a candidate at the forthcoming election. Having been continually a member of the Board for over 17 years, I have repeatedly received expressions of your confidence. and if you again honour me by returning me as a member; I shall endeavour to deserve your confidence in the future, by ever studying the interests of the town, and for- warding its prosperity. I am, Ladies and Gentlemen, Your obedient Servant, SAMUEL TAYLOR.</p>
