ship of Newton-in-Ma kerfleld as is hounded by a line commencing at the point where the 1 Haydock Colliery Railway enters the Township, thence along the said Railway to Crow Lane, thence along and : including the north side of Crow Lane to and including Gas Street, and from thence by the westerly side of the . Brook running in a southerly direction to the boundary ot the Township. So much of the Township of Newton- in-Malterfield as is not included in the Earlestown Poll- ing Districi:, Buttonwood, Houghton, Middleton, and Arhury, Southworth-with-Croft, and Winwick-with- flulme. At the Local Board Offices,ASHTON-IN-MAKERFIELD on Tuesday, the said 26th day ot September next, at three o'clock in the afternoon, for the Townships or places of—Astiton-in-Makerfield and Ilaydock, At Brewis' Schools' GOLBORNE, on Wednesday; the 27th day of'September next, at eleven o'clock in the forenoon, for the Township or Place of Golborne. At the National Schools. BILLINGE CHAPEL END, on Wednesday, the said 27th day of September next, at half-past three o'clock in the afternoon, for the Town- ships or Places of Billinge Chapel End, Billinge Higher End„ Winstanley. And all Overseers of the Poor and other persons hav- ing anything to do at any of the sald several Courts are hereby tequired to attend the same at the said several Times and Places respectively, andy all overseers of the Poor are further required to produce nt tine said Ccurts respectively all Rates made for the relief of the Poor of their respective Parishes or Townships, between the sth .day ofJartuary, 1893. and the 15th day of July, 1893. Dated the 24th day of Auoust; 1883. FREDERICK CAMPBELL FIULTON, Clark of the Peace.</p>
