        <p>• ' EARLESTOWN AND TILE COLLI EltS STRIKE. • It was rumoured on Thursday at Earlestel% that serious fighting had taken place at Celli'', Green Colliery, but enquiry elicited the fart Oa" nothing of the kind had occurred, although ° colliers are determined not to allow any me° descend the pit. Much suffering is being ocCasioned in Earlestn-, and district because of the lock out ot Efforts have however been made to alleviate 0" distress to some extent, and during the pastb-e„: present week, soup, bread, and potatoes have distributed in large quantities to deserving fam• by Mr. M. Winstanley, Mr. Molyneaux, &amp;c., the T. R. Matthews also lending valnable aid. been arranged to hold a meeting of those interes in the work, in the vestry of St. Jotin's Church tcr day (Friday) to consider what had best be clon,eB' It is also on the tapis to give a concert in aid of 0, relief fund. Mr. W. Aspinall, with other worker has interested himself in the good 0,1 and by the kindness of the Committee of the servative Club - has obtained the loan of .kitchen for the purpose of preparing and distrihu,,, ing soup and bland. In this he has been ab' assisted by the gentlemen and tradesmen of town who have given liberally in money and By this means many families have been saved fll7_,'" starvation and the efforts of the Committee 99'0, much appreciated. Up to to-day (Friday). loaves, 260 gallons of soup, and six loads of Wu' have been distributed. The number of people plied daily are as fellow: Monday 161, TriesdBYlo Wednesday 200, Thursday 190, Friday 200. following gentlemen and tradesmen have 000'04 buted in money, Mews. J. W. Thorpe, R, Stone, B. F. Bonen, A.Tunstall, T. Forster, E. T. ecenT, H. Reynolds, R. Roberts, J. Smith, R. Lythgne,a Chorlton' P. Langton, W. Sothern, P. NolOry Allen, T.Molyneux, W. Melling, A. D. A. Smith!ex.r, Ratcliffe, A. Owbridge, T. Hamer, J. Howe, C. Dicoy 4.313800, T. Tunstall. and Mrs. Dickenson. Thehle lowing have contributed beef, bread, vegelol4!, &amp;c. : Messrs P. Naylor, H. Allen, R. Jones, J. Littler, J. Howe, T. Molyneux, W. Sother:ra, Longton. Haslam, T. Sanderson, J. Jones, and `t'Lli'd Lovesay. The Committee superintending' J. arrangements are Messrs. P. Naylor, H. All,erld'io Kynaston, R. Roberts, whilst the follow2ng.,!a„lot, have given assistance, Mesdames Chorlton, Allen, Walton, and Kynaston. Assistance an,' tributions will be gladly received and acknovv'e-roe• by Mr. W. Aspinall, School House, Vitriol Egli</p>
